From 8c88d8bd3859aedd6a013932f5b3a77b85ddeaea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:59:45 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_krdpserver: state first, settings on two sub-pages,
 certificate generation off the GUI thread
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List (allowed users), with the state of the server above it. The two forms that sat in the list's footer
(a ToolBar positioned by a bottomMargin expression) became sub-pages reached from toolbar buttons. Config keys,
kcfg, systemd calls, KWallet use and the phone layout are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Top of the page: "Remote desktop is on/off" (bold) + the addresses while it runs + "Start automatically on login"
  (was "Start server: Automatically on login" in Server Settings). The toolbar switch stays.
- "Server Settings" -> sub-page "Connection Settings…": sections "Connection" (listening port, operating mode) and
  "Video quality" (quality, adaptive quality). "Enable exclusive mode" -> "Exclusive mode"; "Automatically adjust
  quality for network conditions" -> "Adjust quality automatically for network conditions".
- "Security Certificates" -> sub-page "Certificates…" ("Generate certificates: Automatically" -> "Certificate:
  Generate automatically"; paths shown only when not automatic, as before).
- Kirigami.Form replaced by Kirigami.FormLayout on the sub-pages (page-design.md section 2).
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (state and users first), HIG-013/015 (rare options on named sub-pages), HIG-023,
HIG-047 (FormLayout), HIG-057 (no "Advanced"). Page-design.md sections 1, 2, 6, 7.

Speed cause (code evidence): on the first start with "generate automatically" and empty paths the constructor ran
generateCertificate(): QProcess openssl + waitForFinished() on the GUI thread before the first frame. It now uses
QProcess::finished; the result signals are emitted when it exits. The address list called
QNetworkInterface::allInterfaces() in the Repeater model even while hidden; it now waits until the server runs. The
H264 probe (QtConcurrent) and the systemd state (async QDBusPendingCallWatcher) were already asynchronous in master.
Also: m_currentServerStatus is now initialised to Unknown (it was uninitialised, so the first reply could be dropped).
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
